sequenceDiagram
    title BLE GATT Operation Failure and Retry

    participant App as App<br>[implements GattClientResponse]
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GattClient]
    participant Peripheral as BLE Peripheral

    Note over Node, Peripheral: Messages between Node and BLE Peripheral<br>are link-layer / ATT events, not driven by the App.<br>The App only observes them through Echo callbacks.

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Peripheral: Peripheral rejects the write<br>(e.g. insufficient authentication)
        App->>Node: GattClient.WriteCharacteristic(<br>handle=0x0025, data=0x01)
        Node-)Peripheral: ATT_WRITE_REQ (handle=0x0025, value=0x01)
        Peripheral-)Node: ATT_ERROR_RSP (0x05 insufficient authentication)
        Node-->>App: GattClientResponse.OperationComplete(error)
        Note over App, Node: OperationComplete(error) causes:<br>insufficient authentication, write not permitted,<br>invalid handle, invalid offset,<br>attribute-not-found, application error.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Peripheral: Local ATT bearer momentarily busy (retryable)
        App->>Node: GattClient.ReadCharacteristic(0x0025)
        Node-->>App: GattClientResponse.OperationComplete(retry)
        Note over App, Node: retry signals a transient<br>client-side backpressure condition.<br>Re-submit the same call.<br>No state change on the peripheral.

        App->>Node: GattClient.ReadCharacteristic(0x0025)
        Node-)Peripheral: ATT_READ_REQ (handle=0x0025)
        Peripheral-)Node: ATT_READ_RSP (value)
        Node-->>App: GattClientResponse.ReadCharacteristicResponse(<br>data={handle=0x0025, data=0x64})
        Node-->>App: GattClientResponse.OperationComplete(success)
    end
